      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers were Potawatomi of the Algonquin tribe, laying the groundwork before Tekonsha became a village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://tekonshatownship.com/about-us",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A weekly newspaper keeps residents informed, while Union, Baptist, and Church of God churches serve the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
